{:name "storage"
 :version "1.0.0"
 :description "Application-level storage primitives over graphden's own datasource. Distinct from `web/sql`, which uses caller credentials and an isolated external PostgreSQL pool: these base-fns use the platform's own datasource."
 :dependencies ["core"]
 ;; `protocol` must load BEFORE `pg` so the `:Storage` type-row is
 ;; registered before `:postgres-storage-impl` declares it as parent.
 ;; `branches` loads after `pg` — its graph composition uses
 ;; `:pg-query` + `:decode-row` for the branch-chain walk.
 ;; `queue` — the Postgres message queue (SKIP LOCKED + NOTIFY) and the
 ;; graph-level consumer template; after `pg` (raw SQL) like `branches`.
 :modules ["protocol" "pg" "branches" "versioned" "queue"]}
